libqoriq-rcw (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * rcw_pbl_verify(): the verdict such as BootROM would likely do
  * rcw_pbi_to_source(): add the .pbi line of a decoded command
  * rcw_pbl_from_rcw(): RCW[PBI_LENGTH] and RCW[SB_EN] of a bare RCW, as
    the RCWSR registers
  * rcw_ctx_set_bitfield_text(): the -D NAME=VALUE override same as rcw.py
    rcw_ctx_add_define() takes NAME=VALUE as a C compiler does.
  * Exported envelope constants: RCW_PBL_PREAMBLE, RCW_PBL_CMD_LOAD_RCW,
    RCW_PBL_CMD_LOAD_RCW_NOCS, RCW_PBL_TERMINATOR_BYTES.
  * An invalid bitfield value is reported on stderr unconditionally, no
    longer only with warnings enabled.

 -- Vincent Jardin <vjardin@free.fr>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:32:45 +0200

libqoriq-rcw (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Image checking API: rcw_pbi_decode, rcw_pbi_op_name, rcw_pbl_parse,
    rcw_pbi_crc and rcw_pbl_check, with RCW_ERR_TRUNCATED and
    RCW_ERR_PBI_LENGTH.
  * PBI: loadc, jump, jumpc and labels as upstream rcw.py spells them,
    printed back with labels by the decompiler; loadcondition and
    jumpif kept as aliases.
  * PBI: awrite.b1 to awrite.b10, every AltConfig Write width.
  * PBI: operands evaluated like Python's eval(); trailing text and
    results outside 32 bits are errors. flush refused under pbiformat=2.
  * Parse: numbers read as Python's int(x, 0); %sysaddr refused with
    pbiformat=2.
  * Preprocess: rcw_ctx_add_define() for -D macros (RCW_CPPFLAGS).
  * Decompile: list the set bits no field covers.
  * Binary: Load RCW checksum summed in the image's word order.

 -- Vincent Jardin <vjardin@free.fr>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:09:54 +0200

libqoriq-rcw (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * PBI: the command set is now feature complete. New mnemonics for
    conditional execution (loadcondition 0x14, jump 0x84, jumpif 0x85),
    for the density commands (ccsrcopy 0x02, ccsrset / ccsrclear /
    ccsrreplace 0x42) and for secure boot (loadsecurityheader 0x20,
    loadboot1csfptr 0x22), on both the compile and decompile paths.
  * PBI: poll now emits the four words described by the reference
    manual.
  * Decompile: awrite keeps its width suffix.
  * Compile: warn when the generated PBL reaches 4096 bytes; 4092 is
    the measured LX2160A Service Processor ceiling above which the SoC
    stays silent.
  * Tests: new test_cond, test_density and test_secure suites, plus
    coverage for flush.

 -- Vincent Jardin <vjardin@free.fr>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 00:52:20 +0200

